And some of my favorites? Tourists are great fun! Wander around, taking
pictures of everything! Harder then hell to play, but if you can start off
with some spinich, and get a good strength boost from it, things go
pretty good.
Archaeologists are also fun, simply because I *LOVE* knowing what all
the gems are (I'm a sucker for collecting the damn things) and speed
is very handy on the beginning levels.
Rogues, though I don't play often, I kinda like too, since searching is
my favorite intrinsic.
Healers are tough, but the stethoscope is nice, as is the wand of sleep,
and healing stuff, for avoiding an early death. But once they run out,
if you've not found decent armour, and a weapon, things get ugly
(especially since they have such horrendous combat stats *ick*)
Gotta love being immunized.  =)
Knights too are handy, being lawful with a longsword is great, if you
can live long enough to take advantage of it. My only ascension is with
a Knight.
Cavemen are my hack and slash player of choice, if I don't feel like
struggling to live through the first few levels.

Overall, tourists are my favorite, followed by vegetarian valkyries.
